# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> no false merge conflict on registration.
# register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_schema_large_file.py" "SCHEMA LARGE-FILE GATE: PASS" "schema large-file recall" "schema-aware file-size cap: a whole-DB DDL dump (Rails/GitLab db/structure.sql, legitimately > the 1.5MB general cap) IS parsed so its tables enter the graph (recall win, measured: GitLab's ~2.9MB schema = 0 tables before -> 1475 after); the exception is .sql-specific (a >1.5MB .py is still skipped) and still BOUNDED (.sql above _SCHEMA_FILE_SIZE_CAP=12MB skipped, no pathological-dump read); a renamed binary is still caught by _is_binary" "large .sql schema dumps no longer silently skipped (enterprise/Rails recall) while general + pathological caps stay intact" 30
